-- title:
--   Chart rings of a tower quotient datum over affine opens
-- statement:
--   Let $\mathcal O$ be a commutative domain which is a discrete valuation ring, $\pi \in \mathcal O$ irreducible, and $\mathcal O$ complete for the $\pi$-adic topology. Let $(X_n)_{n\ge 0}$ be schemes with structure morphisms $xb_n : X_n \to \operatorname{Spec}(\mathcal O/\pi^{n+1})$ and transitions $xt_n : X_n \to X_{n+1}$ making each square over $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the projection $\mathcal O/\pi^{n+2} \to \mathcal O/\pi^{n+1}$ cartesian, with every $xb_n$ proper and flat; let $G$ be a finite group acting on each $X_n$ by automorphisms over the base and commuting with the $xt_n$. Let $D$ be a tower quotient datum: schemes $Y_n$ with proper flat structure maps $yb_n$ to $\operatorname{Spec}(\mathcal O/\pi^{n+1})$ and cartesian transitions $yt_n$, together with morphisms $p_n : X_n \to Y_n$ over the base, compatible with the transitions, with $(xt_n, p_n, p_{n+1}, yt_n)$ cartesian, invariant under $G$, finite, surjective, remaining epimorphic after restriction over any open of $Y_n$, and satisfying the local universal property of the quotient recorded in `univ_loc`. Finally let $V_n \subseteq Y_n$ be affine opens with $yt_n^{-1}(V_{n+1}) = V_n$. Then there exist a commutative ring $R$, an $\mathcal O$-algebra structure on it and an action of $G$ on $R$ by ring automorphisms commuting with the $\mathcal O$-scalars, such that $R$ is complete for the ideal generated by the image of $\pi$, the image of $\pi$ is a non-zero-divisor in $R$, the quotient $R/\pi R$ is an $\mathcal O$-algebra of finite type, and there are ring isomorphisms $\mathrm{lvl}_n : R/\pi^{n+1}R \xrightarrow{\sim} \Gamma(X_n, p_n^{-1}V_n)$ and $\mu_n : A/\pi^{n+1}A \xrightarrow{\sim} \Gamma(Y_n, V_n)$, where $A$ is the $\mathcal O$-subalgebra of $G$-fixed points of $R$, subject to six compatibilities: the $\mathrm{lvl}_n$ commute with the restriction maps induced by $xt_n$ on these preimages; $\mathrm{lvl}_n$ carries the action of $g \in G$ on $R$ to the map induced on sections by the automorphism attached to $g^{-1}$; $\mathrm{lvl}_n$ sends the image of $o \in \mathcal O$ to the pullback along $xb_n$ of the class of $o$ in $\mathcal O/\pi^{n+1}$ viewed as a global section of $\operatorname{Spec}(\mathcal O/\pi^{n+1})$; the $\mu_n$ commute with the restriction maps induced by $yt_n$; pulling back along $p_n$ takes $\mu_n$ to $\mathrm{lvl}_n$ composed with the inclusion $A \hookrightarrow R$; and $\mu_n$ sends the image of $o \in \mathcal O$ to the pullback along $yb_n$ of the class of $o$.
--
--   This is the local chart description of a tower quotient datum: over a compatible chain of affine opens $V_n$ of the quotient tower, the sections of the preimages assemble into a single $\pi$-adically complete, $\pi$-torsion-free $\mathcal O$-algebra $R$ with $G$-action whose ring of invariants computes the sections over the $V_n$. It is used in the proof of [`AlgebraicGeometry.TowerQuotientDatum.univ_loc_of_isPullback_of_flat`](thm.html#AlgebraicGeometry.TowerQuotientDatum.univ_loc_of_isPullback_of_flat), where the universal property of the quotient tower is verified by reduction to these affine charts.
